	(text "Goal: unplug the remote and the Micra's paddle works as stock. The USB-C 5 V (J3) only passes through F1 (1.5 A PTC) to the remote on J1; every LED is still driven straight from a remote GPIO.\nCTRL (GPIO50) low or floating -> U2/U3 NC switches closed (paddle wired to the Micra in copper), NO switches open, remote fully disconnected.\nCTRL high (firmware, Wired paddle on) -> NC open, NO closed: paddle reads on SENSE (GPIO51), U1 alone drives the Micra from DRIVE (GPIO52)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1424ceb9-b2a1-4b21-aab1-b4547c4e8e2f")
	)
	(text "BOM: U2/U3 = Vishay LH1502BB (DIP-8) dual 1-Form-A/B SSR used as 1-Form-C (350 V, 150 mA, 20 R typ, 3750 Vrms). Pinout per Vishay 83806: 1/2 = LED for the S1 switch (8/7 = NC),\n3/4 = LED for the S2 switch (6/5 = NO); common made on the board by tying 7 to 6. LED must-operate is 2 mA MAX for both switches, so R2-R5 = 330R: ~6.4 mA nominal each,\n3.6 mA worst case (VOH 2.64 V, Vf 1.45 V) = 1.8x margin; ~26 mA total on CTRL -> set GPIO50 to PAD_DRIVER 3 (40 mA class, P4 datasheet 5.4).\nU1 = Panasonic AQY212EH (DIP-4) 1-Form-A PhotoMOS (60 V, 550 mA, 3 mA max operate), R1 330R. Bidirectional output = no polarity on the Micra plug.\nR6 1k = the series protection resistor the wiring guide already recommends. R7+D1 = optional stronger SENSE pull-up, present only while CTRL is high.\nLED1+R8 = optional 'remote in control' indicator. Footprints: 1206 passives; U1 DIP-4, U2/U3 DIP-8 through-hole so the Panasonic AQW612EH (same pinout: 8/7 = N.C., 6/5 = N.O.)\nis a drop-in for U2/U3 with R2-R5 changed to 270R (3 mA LED); J1/J2 JST PH 4-pin side-entry (S4B-PH-K; same drills as the vertical B4B-PH-K)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 178 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "165c7af5-c8d3-48e7-8157-ef59952efd1f")
	)
	(text "APOLLO PADDLE BRIDGE - rev 0.6 (2026-09-24)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1de0b581-ecd6-49d4-8400-543d906cd15e")
	)
	(text "FIRMWARE: one new output, kPaddleCtrlPin per board (GPIO50 on the P4-5/4.3, GPIO46 on the X boxes), HIGH while Wired paddle is on and the app\nis running, LOW otherwise and in install mode. Drive strength max (gpio_set_drive_capability). New 'padctrl' NVS remap key beside padsense/paddrive."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 186.69 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9addfe76-f034-4c8d-8c32-c0e9e0730e0f")
	)
	(text "ISOLATION: MICRA_W / MICRA_B / P1 / P2 touch only relay outputs. GND_R is the remote's ground and never reaches the Micra side.\nThe paddle island (P1/P2) belongs to the Micra when CTRL is low and to the remote when CTRL is high - never both. All SSRs rated -40..+85 C (in-chassis OK, not on the boiler)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a5561e57-2b86-42d2-b3c5-e92a074d763d")
	)
